#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ccfleet -- run headless Claude Code sessions across a fleet of repos, each
one billed to its own repo, started only while the machine has headroom.

Why it exists: per-repo cost tools (`ccrepo`) label usage by the session's
working-directory basename. A subagent started with the Agent tool runs in its
parent's directory, so work done "for" another repo by an Agent subagent bills
the orchestrator's repo, not the repo it was for. The fix is structural: each
repo's work runs as its own `claude -p` session started INSIDE a worktree of
that repo whose basename is the repo name. Doing that by hand for a dozen repos,
without crashing the machine, is what this instrument does.

THE LESSONS IT CARRIES (each one paid for in a real run):
  * `claude -p` is always started with stdin from /dev/null. Without it a
    "no stdin" warning lands in the JSON log and the result cannot be parsed.
  * Every launch names its model (`--model`). A launch without one silently
    inherits the default tier; tools/modelguard.py blocks such launches.
  * The worktree's basename is the repo name, under a per-job parent directory
    (`<worktrees_root>/<label>-<HHMM>/<repo>`). That basename is the billing key.
  * Never repo work as an Agent subagent of the orchestrator (see above).
  * A public repo's prompt never names a private repo. Rendering refuses to
    launch a prompt for a public (or unknown-visibility) repo that contains any
    configured private name. The guard is a literal match, so it catches the
    names you list and nothing you forgot to list.
  * This is Python, not zsh, on purpose: zsh reads a script as it runs, so
    editing a driver script mid-run broke every running job's tail. Python
    compiles the whole file at start, so a running driver is immune; a job
    started after an edit runs the edited copy.
  * Start one job at a time, staggered, and only while load, free memory and
    free disk all have headroom: parallel test runs inside headless sessions
    have taken a 16 GB laptop past load 100. Workers run their own tests
    niced and single-process; say so in the prompt.
  * A run past a usage limit ends with no RESULT line (read as UNKNOWN). The
    drain stops after three unclean ends in a row, which is how a spent budget
    shows up from outside.
  * Every session runs with CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS=0. Without
    it `claude -p` kills a background subagent about ten minutes after the
    orchestrator's last turn, so a reviewer working on act 2 died mid-act.
  * `claude -p` prints only the last turn. A session whose last turn followed
    a background notification printed no RESULT line though its report was
    written; the harvest then reads the session's own transcript.
  * A `touch <kit_dir>/stop` ends launching cleanly; running jobs finish. A
    stop file older than the driver is ignored (and logged): last week's file
    once ended a new run before it started anything.
  * The ceiling is live: <kit_dir>/max holds it while a driver runs; edit the
    number to pace a run without stopping it.
  * Children start in their own session, so closing the driver's terminal
    does not end the sessions it started.

Usage:
  ccfleet check                       validate the config and print what it resolves to
  ccfleet gate                        print the headroom reading; exit 0 if a start may go now
  ccfleet run REPO --prompt FILE [--label L] [--model M] [--set K=V ...] [--keep] [--in WT] [--dry-run]
  ccfleet drive JOBS [--max N] [--serial-per-repo] [--dry-run]
  ccfleet drain [--max N] [--dry-run]
  ccfleet pass REPO ITEM BRIEF [--dry-run]      one drain pass (drain starts these)
  ccfleet resume REPO WORKTREE SESSION --prompt FILE [--item ITEM] [--set K=V ...]
  common: --config PATH (else $CCFLEET_CONFIG)  --by ID (else $CCFLEET_BY): the
  orchestrating session's id, filled into prompts as {BY}.

JOBS is a TSV file, one job per line: repo, label, prompt template, then any
number of KEY=VALUE fields that fill {KEY} in that template (MODEL=<id> sets the
model; a value written @file:PATH takes that file's text, for a multi-line
task). '#' lines and blank lines are skipped. A job whose result file for today
already exists is skipped, so re-running a drive resumes it.

CONFIG is JSON (see instruments/ccfleet.example.json, every value fictional):
  kit_dir         logs/, results/<date>/, scratch/<repo>/, the stop file   (required)
  repos_root      primary checkouts live at <repos_root>/<repo>          (required)
  worktrees_root  job worktrees go under here                            (required)
  default_model   the model a job runs on when neither job nor repo names one (required)
  claude_bin      default "claude";   claude_args  extra args, e.g. a permission mode
  nice            default 5;  max_concurrent  default 4;  stagger_seconds  default 90;  poll_seconds 30
  gate            {max_load (default 2 x cores), min_mem_pct 25, min_disk_gb 20}
  reset_utc       "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM": no new start at or after it (a budget reset)
  private_names   names a public repo's prompt must never contain
  vars            template variables for every job (the principal's words, paths)
  env             extra environment variables for every session (NAME: value)
  repos           {name: {model, notes, visibility, github}}  per-repo facts
  queue           drain only: {next, take, release[, ended]} argv lists, and
                  release_on / stop_on lists of RESULT words (see below)
  pass_prompt     drain only: the per-pass orchestrator prompt template
  pass_model      drain only: the orchestrator's model (the reviewer's tier is the prompt's business)

THE QUEUE INTERFACE (drain). The review queue itself is the adopter's own tool;
ccfleet only calls it. Each entry is an argv list; {REPO} {ITEM} {BRIEF} {BY}
{WT} {LOG} are filled in before the call.
  next     prints "REPO ITEM BRIEF_RELPATH" for the next pass to run, or nothing
           when the queue is empty; tab-separated when a field may hold a
           space. It is called with the launched list's path in {LAUNCHED}
           (one tab-separated "REPO ITEM BRIEF" per line) so it can skip them.
  take     claims the pass; a nonzero exit means someone else holds it (skip).
  release  frees the claim after a pass ends with a RESULT in release_on
           (default DONE, SKIPPED); a refusal is printed and, for resume, exit 2.
  ended    optional: called after every pass or resume, any RESULT, with
           {SESSION} {RESULT} {LOG} {WT} filled (to record them on the claim).
  stop_on  RESULT words that stop the drain (default BUDGET EXHAUSTED).

Template variables always filled: {REPO} {GH} {BR} {VIS} {PIN} {WT} {PRIMARY}
{LANDING} {NOTES} {SCRATCH} {BY} {DATE}, plus config `vars`, plus the job's own.
{PIN}, when the template uses it and nothing supplies it, is the repo's atelier
pin (tools/pins.py, else the CLAUDE.md atelier@<sha>), else UNRESOLVED.
A {UPPER_CASE} placeholder left unfilled is a refusal, not a silent gap.

Exit codes: 0 ran (the session's own verdict is in its END line and result
file) · 1 setup failed · 2 claim refused (or a release refused) · 3 reset
reached · 4 queue empty (a drain that started nothing) · 5 refused by the
private-name guard or an unfilled placeholder · 64 usage.
Runtime: Python 3.8 or later, standard library only; git on PATH; gh optional
(visibility lookup when a repo's config does not state it).
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import glob
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

EXIT_SETUP, EXIT_CLAIM, EXIT_RESET, EXIT_EMPTY, EXIT_GUARD, EXIT_USAGE = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 64
PLACEHOLDER = re.compile(r"\{([A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*)\}")
RESULT_RX = re.compile(r"RESULT:\s*\**\s*([A-Z]+(?: [A-Z]+)?)")
PIN_RX = re.compile(r"atelier@([0-9a-f]{7,40})\b", re.I)
# Without this, `claude -p` kills a background subagent about ten minutes after
# the orchestrator's last turn: a reviewer still working on act 2 dies mid-act.
CEILING_VAR = "CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS"
RELEASE_ON = ["DONE", "SKIPPED"]
STOP_ON = ["BUDGET EXHAUSTED"]


class Refusal(Exception):
    def __init__(self, code, msg):
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.code = code


def now_utc():
    return dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)


def expand(p):
    return os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(p)) if p else p


# ---------- config ----------

def load_config(path):
    path = path or os.environ.get("CCFLEET_CONFIG")
    if not path:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, "no config: pass --config PATH or set CCFLEET_CONFIG")
    with open(expand(path), encoding="utf-8") as f:
        cfg = json.load(f)
    missing = [k for k in ("kit_dir", "repos_root", "worktrees_root", "default_model") if not cfg.get(k)]
    if missing:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, f"config {path}: missing {', '.join(missing)}")
    for k in ("kit_dir", "repos_root", "worktrees_root"):
        cfg[k] = expand(cfg[k])
    cfg.setdefault("claude_bin", "claude")
    cfg.setdefault("claude_args", [])
    cfg.setdefault("nice", 5)
    cfg.setdefault("max_concurrent", 4)
    cfg.setdefault("stagger_seconds", 90)
    cfg.setdefault("poll_seconds", 30)
    gate = cfg.setdefault("gate", {})
    gate.setdefault("max_load", 2 * (os.cpu_count() or 4))
    gate.setdefault("min_mem_pct", 25)
    gate.setdefault("min_disk_gb", 20)
    cfg.setdefault("private_names", [])
    cfg.setdefault("vars", {})
    cfg.setdefault("repos", {})
    if not isinstance(cfg.setdefault("env", {}), dict):
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, f"config {path}: env must be an object of NAME: value")
    q = cfg.get("queue") or {}
    for k, default in (("release_on", RELEASE_ON), ("stop_on", STOP_ON)):
        if not isinstance(q.get(k, default), list):
            raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, f"config {path}: queue.{k} must be a list of RESULT words")
    return cfg


def release_on(cfg):
    return list((cfg.get("queue") or {}).get("release_on", RELEASE_ON))


def stop_on(cfg):
    return list((cfg.get("queue") or {}).get("stop_on", STOP_ON))


def reset_reached(cfg, at=None):
    r = cfg.get("reset_utc")
    if not r:
        return False
    when = dt.datetime.strptime(r, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M").replace(tzinfo=dt.timezone.utc)
    return (at or now_utc()) >= when


# ---------- headroom gate ----------

def read_mem_pct():
    """Free memory as a percentage, or None when it cannot be read."""
    if sys.platform == "darwin":
        try:
            out = subprocess.run(["memory_pressure", "-Q"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20).stdout
            m = re.search(r"free percentage:\s*(\d+)", out)
            return int(m.group(1)) if m else None
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            return None
    try:
        info = {}
        with open("/proc/meminfo") as f:
            for line in f:
                k, v = line.split(":", 1)
                info[k] = int(v.split()[0])
        return int(100 * info["MemAvailable"] / info["MemTotal"])
    except (OSError, KeyError, ValueError):
        return None


def read_headroom(cfg):
    l1, l5, l15 = os.getloadavg()
    probe = cfg["worktrees_root"]
    while not os.path.exists(probe):
        probe = os.path.dirname(probe)
    disk_gb = shutil.disk_usage(probe).free // 2**30
    return {"load": (l1, l5, l15), "mem_pct": read_mem_pct(), "disk_gb": disk_gb}


def gate_ok(gate, reading):
    """A start may go only when every reading has headroom. An unreadable
    memory figure holds (fail closed) unless min_mem_pct is 0."""
    l1, l5, _ = reading["load"]
    if l1 >= gate["max_load"] or l5 >= gate["max_load"]:
        return False
    if gate["min_mem_pct"] > 0 and (reading["mem_pct"] is None or reading["mem_pct"] < gate["min_mem_pct"]):
        return False
    return reading["disk_gb"] >= gate["min_disk_gb"]


def describe(reading):
    l = reading["load"]
    mem = "?" if reading["mem_pct"] is None else reading["mem_pct"]
    return f"load {l[0]:.1f}/{l[1]:.1f}/{l[2]:.1f} mem {mem}% disk {reading['disk_gb']}G"


# ---------- git facts ----------

def git(*args, cwd=None, check=True):
    r = subprocess.run(["git", *args], cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"git {' '.join(args)}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return r.stdout.strip()


def repo_facts(cfg, repo, fetch=True):
    primary = os.path.join(cfg["repos_root"], repo)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(primary, ".git")) and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(primary, ".git")):
        raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"not a git checkout: {primary}")
    rc = cfg["repos"].get(repo, {})
    remote = git("remote", "get-url", "origin", cwd=primary, check=False)
    facts = {"primary": primary, "remote": bool(remote)}
    if remote:
        if fetch:
            git("fetch", "-q", "origin", cwd=primary)
        # Not every repo's mainline is main.
        ref = git("symbolic-ref", "--short", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD", cwd=primary, check=False)
        facts["defref"] = ref or "origin/main"
        facts["branch"] = facts["defref"].split("/", 1)[1]
        m = re.search(r"github\.com[:/](.+?)(?:\.git)?$", remote)
        facts["gh"] = rc.get("github") or (m.group(1) if m else remote)
    else:
        facts["defref"] = facts["branch"] = rc.get("branch", "main")
        facts["gh"] = rc.get("github", "(no remote)")
    vis = rc.get("visibility")
    if not vis and remote and shutil.which("gh") and fetch:
        r = subprocess.run(["gh", "repo", "view", facts["gh"], "--json", "visibility", "-q", ".visibility"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        vis = r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else None
    facts["visibility"] = (vis or "UNKNOWN").upper()
    return facts


def landing_text(facts, wt, branch_name=None):
    if facts["remote"]:
        b = facts["branch"]
        return (f"Land each commit with `git -C '{wt}' pull --rebase origin {b}` then "
                f"`git -C '{wt}' push origin HEAD:{b}` (unless this repo's CLAUDE.md requires "
                f"a PR; then open one and say so).")
    return (f"This repo has NO remote; local {facts['branch']} is the mainline and your worktree is on "
            f"branch {branch_name}. Instead of pull/push: `git -C '{wt}' rebase {facts['branch']}`, then land "
            f"with `git -C '{facts['primary']}' merge --ff-only {branch_name}` against the primary checkout "
            f"(only while it is on {facts['branch']}; if the merge refuses over uncommitted changes there, "
            f"wait and retry, never stash or absorb them). Never `git push`.")


# ---------- prompt rendering ----------

def render(template, values):
    out = PLACEHOLDER.sub(lambda m: str(values[m.group(1)]) if m.group(1) in values else m.group(0), template)
    left = sorted(set(PLACEHOLDER.findall(out)))
    return out, left


def private_hits(cfg, text, visibility):
    """Private names in a prompt bound for a public or unknown-visibility repo."""
    if visibility == "PRIVATE":
        return []
    names = set(cfg["private_names"])
    names |= {r for r, rc in cfg["repos"].items() if str(rc.get("visibility", "")).upper() == "PRIVATE"}
    return sorted(n for n in names if re.search(r"(?<![\w-])" + re.escape(n) + r"(?![\w-])", text, re.I))


def build_prompt(cfg, template_path, values, template_text=None):
    if template_text is None:
        template_text = read_template(template_path)
    text, left = render(template_text, values)
    if left:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_GUARD, f"unfilled placeholder(s) in {template_path}: {', '.join('{'+k+'}' for k in left)}")
    hits = private_hits(cfg, text, values.get("VIS", "UNKNOWN"))
    if hits:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_GUARD, f"refused: the prompt for {values.get('REPO')} ({values.get('VIS')}) names "
                                  f"private name(s) {', '.join(hits)}")
    return text


# ---------- one session ----------

def config_dir():
    """Claude Code's own directory: $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, else ~/.claude."""
    return expand(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or "~/.claude")


def message_text(msg):
    """The text blocks of a transcript message, joined."""
    if not isinstance(msg, dict):
        return ""
    c = msg.get("content")
    if isinstance(c, str):
        return c
    if isinstance(c, list):
        return "\n".join(b.get("text", "") for b in c if isinstance(b, dict) and b.get("type") == "text")
    return ""


def transcript_result(sid, since=None):
    """The newest assistant text carrying a RESULT: line in the session's own
    transcript (<config dir>/projects/*/<sid>.jsonl), or "". Entries stamped
    before `since` (ISO UTC) are not read, so a resumed session never takes an
    earlier run's verdict."""
    if not sid or not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+", sid):
        return ""
    best = ("", -1, "")
    for path in glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(config_dir()), "projects", "*", sid + ".jsonl")):
        try:
            with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
                lines = f.readlines()
        except OSError:
            continue
        for n, line in enumerate(lines):
            try:
                e = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if not isinstance(e, dict) or e.get("type") != "assistant":
                continue
            ts = str(e.get("timestamp") or "")
            if since and ts and ts < since:
                continue
            text = message_text(e.get("message"))
            if RESULT_RX.search(text) and (ts, n) >= best[:2]:
                best = (ts, n, text)
    return best[2]


def harvest(log_path, since=None):
    """(result text, session id, RESULT word) from a `claude -p --output-format json` log.
    `claude -p` prints only the last turn. A session whose last turn came after
    a background notification (a subagent finishing) can print a line with no
    RESULT in it while its real report sits earlier; then the transcript is
    read for the newest assistant text that has one."""
    try:
        with open(log_path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            s = f.read()
    except OSError:
        return "", "", "UNKNOWN"
    try:
        j = json.loads(s[s.index("{"):])
        text, sid = j.get("result", "") or "", j.get("session_id", "") or ""
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        text, sid = s[-4000:], ""
    found = RESULT_RX.findall(text)
    if not found and sid:
        t = transcript_result(sid, since)
        if t:
            text = "(read from the session transcript: the last turn printed no RESULT line)\n" + t
            found = RESULT_RX.findall(t)
    return text, sid, (found[-1] if found else "UNKNOWN")


def stamp_dir(root, label):
    stamp = now_utc().strftime("%H%M")
    parent = os.path.join(root, f"{label}-{stamp}")
    if os.path.exists(parent):
        parent += now_utc().strftime("%S")
    return parent


def session_argv(cfg, model, prompt, resume=None):
    argv = []
    if cfg["nice"]:
        argv += ["nice", "-n", str(cfg["nice"])]
    argv += [cfg["claude_bin"], "-p"]
    if resume:
        argv += ["--resume", resume]
    argv += ["--model", model, *cfg["claude_args"], "--output-format", "json", prompt]
    return argv


def session_env(cfg):
    """The launch environment: ours, the config's `env`, and the wait ceiling
    switched off, always (see CEILING_VAR)."""
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env.update({str(k): str(v) for k, v in cfg.get("env", {}).items()})
    env[CEILING_VAR] = "0"
    return env


def launch(cfg, argv, cwd, log):
    # stdin from /dev/null, always: see the module docstring.
    with open(log, "w") as out, open(log + ".err", "w") as err:
        return subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=out, stderr=err,
                              env=session_env(cfg)).returncode


def iso_now():
    return f"{now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S}"


def read_at_file(v):
    """A variable written `@file:PATH` takes the file's text (a multi-line task)."""
    if isinstance(v, str) and v.startswith("@file:"):
        with open(expand(v[6:]), encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return f.read().rstrip("\n")
    return v


def safe(s):
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]+", "-", s).strip("-")


def resolve_pin(cfg, facts):
    """(pin, source) for a repo: tools/pins.py's reading of its checkout, else
    the first atelier@<sha> in its CLAUDE.md on the mainline (or in the
    checkout), else ("UNRESOLVED", why). Atelier is vars.ATELIER, else the
    checkout this file lives in."""
    atelier = expand(cfg["vars"].get("ATELIER") or
                     os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))))
    pins = os.path.join(atelier, "tools", "pins.py")
    primary = facts["primary"]
    if os.path.isfile(pins):
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, pins, "--atelier", atelier, "--head", "--child", primary,
                                "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120,
                               stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
            kids = json.loads(r.stdout).get("children") or []
            if kids and kids[0].get("pin"):
                return str(kids[0]["pin"]).lower(), "pins.py"
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError, AttributeError):
            pass
    text = git("show", f"{facts['defref']}:CLAUDE.md", cwd=primary, check=False)
    if not text:
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(primary, "CLAUDE.md"), encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
                text = f.read()
        except OSError:
            text = ""
    m = PIN_RX.search(text)
    if m:
        return m.group(1).lower(), "CLAUDE.md"
    why = "pins.py found none" if os.path.isfile(pins) else f"no {pins}"
    return "UNRESOLVED", f"{why}, and CLAUDE.md has no atelier@<sha>"


def base_values(cfg, repo, facts, wt, by, extra, template_text, branch_name=None):
    """Every template value a session gets. {PIN} is resolved only when the
    template uses it and nothing supplied it; an unresolved pin is filled as
    UNRESOLVED and said, never left silently empty."""
    scratch = os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "scratch", safe(repo))
    values = {**{k: str(v) for k, v in cfg["vars"].items()}, **{k: str(v) for k, v in extra.items()},
              "REPO": repo, "GH": facts["gh"], "BR": facts["branch"], "VIS": facts["visibility"],
              "WT": wt, "PRIMARY": facts["primary"], "LANDING": landing_text(facts, wt, branch_name),
              "NOTES": cfg["repos"].get(repo, {}).get("notes", "none"), "SCRATCH": scratch + "/",
              "BY": by, "DATE": f"{now_utc():%Y-%m-%d}"}
    if "PIN" not in values and "{PIN}" in template_text:
        values["PIN"], source = resolve_pin(cfg, facts)
        if values["PIN"] == "UNRESOLVED":
            print(f"PIN UNRESOLVED for {repo}: {source}; the prompt says UNRESOLVED", flush=True)
        else:
            print(f"PIN {values['PIN']} for {repo} (from {source})", flush=True)
    values.setdefault("PIN", "")
    return values


def read_template(path):
    with open(expand(path), encoding="utf-8") as f:
        return f.read()


def run_one(cfg, repo, template, label=None, model=None, extra=None, by="unknown",
            dry=False, keep=False, pre=None, post=None, check_file=None, existing=None,
            clean=("DONE", "SKIPPED")):
    """Make the worktree, render, launch, harvest, clean up. Returns (exit, RESULT word).
    With a `post` hook, the worktree is removed only for a RESULT in `clean`."""
    if reset_reached(cfg):
        print(f"RESET reached; not starting {label or repo}")
        return EXIT_RESET, "RESET"
    extra = {k: read_at_file(v) for k, v in (extra or {}).items()}
    model = model or extra.pop("MODEL", None) or cfg["repos"].get(repo, {}).get("model") or cfg["default_model"]
    label = safe(label or repo)
    facts = repo_facts(cfg, repo, fetch=not dry)
    day = now_utc().strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    wt = expand(existing) if existing else os.path.join(stamp_dir(cfg["worktrees_root"], label), repo)
    if existing and (os.path.basename(wt) != repo or not os.path.isdir(wt)):
        # The basename is the billing key: a session in a differently named
        # directory would bill some other label.
        raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"--in must be an existing worktree whose basename is {repo}: {wt}")
    keep = keep or bool(existing)  # an adopted worktree is the caller's to remove
    kit = cfg["kit_dir"]
    logs, results, scratch = (os.path.join(kit, "logs"), os.path.join(kit, "results", day),
                              os.path.join(kit, "scratch", safe(repo)))
    log = os.path.join(logs, os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(wt))
                       + (f"-in-{now_utc():%H%M%S}" if existing else "") + ".json")
    branch_name = None if (facts["remote"] or existing) else f"fleet/{label}-{now_utc().strftime('%H%M%S')}"
    template_text = read_template(template)
    values = base_values(cfg, repo, facts, wt, by, extra, template_text, branch_name)
    prompt = build_prompt(cfg, template, values, template_text)
    argv = session_argv(cfg, model, prompt)
    if dry:
        print(f"DRY {repo} model={model} vis={facts['visibility']} wt={wt}")
        print(f"DRY worktree add from {facts['defref']}; log={log}")
        print("DRY argv: " + " ".join(argv[:-1]) + f" <prompt {len(prompt)} chars> < /dev/null")
        return 0, "DRY"
    for d in (logs, results, scratch, os.path.dirname(wt)):
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    if existing:
        pass
    elif facts["remote"]:
        git("worktree", "add", "-q", "--detach", wt, facts["defref"], cwd=facts["primary"])
    else:
        git("worktree", "add", "-q", "-b", branch_name, wt, facts["branch"], cwd=facts["primary"])

    def cleanup():
        git("worktree", "remove", "--force", wt, cwd=facts["primary"], check=False)
        try:
            os.rmdir(os.path.dirname(wt))
        except OSError:
            pass
        if branch_name:
            git("branch", "-d", branch_name, cwd=facts["primary"], check=False)

    if check_file and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(wt, check_file)):
        print(f"not on {facts['defref']}: {check_file}")
        cleanup()
        return EXIT_SETUP, "UNKNOWN"
    if pre:
        code = pre(values, log)
        if code:
            cleanup()
            return code, "UNKNOWN"
    print(f"START {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} {label} model={model} wt={wt} log={log}", flush=True)
    since = iso_now()
    rc = launch(cfg, argv, wt, log)
    text, sid, result = harvest(log, since)
    out = os.path.join(results, f"{label}.md")
    with open(out, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(f"<!-- session {sid} -->\n{text}\n")
    print(f"END {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} rc={rc} result={result} session={sid} out={out}", flush=True)
    if post:
        post(values, result, sid, log)
    if not keep and (result in clean or not post):
        cleanup()
    return 0, result


# ---------- drivers ----------

class DriverLock:
    """One driver per kit_dir: two drivers would each think they own the slots."""

    def __init__(self, kit):
        self.path = os.path.join(kit, "driver.pid")

    def __enter__(self):
        if os.path.exists(self.path):
            try:
                with open(self.path) as f:
                    pid = int(f.read().strip())
                os.kill(pid, 0)
                raise Refusal(EXIT_SETUP, f"another driver (pid {pid}) is running on this kit_dir")
            except (ValueError, ProcessLookupError):
                pass
        with open(self.path, "w") as f:
            f.write(str(os.getpid()))
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        try:
            os.remove(self.path)
        except OSError:
            pass


def say(cfg, msg):
    with open(os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "driver.log"), "a") as f:
        f.write(f"{now_utc():%H:%MZ} {msg}\n")


def read_jobs(path):
    jobs = []
    with open(expand(path), encoding="utf-8") as f:
        lines = f.read().splitlines()
    for n, line in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if not line.strip() or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        f = line.split("\t")
        if len(f) < 3:
            raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, f"{path}:{n}: need repo, label, prompt")
        extra = dict(x.split("=", 1) for x in f[3:] if "=" in x)
        jobs.append({"repo": f[0], "label": safe(f[1] or f[0]), "prompt": f[2], "vars": extra})
    return jobs


def self_argv(args_common, *rest):
    return [sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), *args_common, *rest]


def spawn(argv, out_path):
    """A child ccfleet in its own session, so it and its `claude` survive the
    driver's terminal closing (a hangup goes to the terminal's session only)."""
    with open(out_path, "w") as out:
        return subprocess.Popen(argv, stdout=out, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                start_new_session=True)


class Pacing:
    """What a driver re-reads every loop: the stop file and the live ceiling.

    The stop file counts only when written after this driver started: one left
    by an earlier run is ignored, and the log says so once. The ceiling is the
    file <kit_dir>/max, written with the starting value when the driver starts
    and removed when it ends; edit the number mid-run to lower or raise it
    (0 holds every new start). Running sessions are never stopped by it."""

    def __init__(self, cfg, max_n):
        self.cfg, self.n = cfg, max_n
        self.started = int(time.time())  # whole seconds: a coarse mtime still compares right
        self.stop_path = os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "stop")
        self.max_path = os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "max")
        self.said_stale = self.said_bad = False
        with open(self.max_path, "w") as f:
            f.write(f"{max_n}\n")

    def stop(self):
        try:
            m = os.path.getmtime(self.stop_path)
        except OSError:
            return False
        if m < self.started:
            if not self.said_stale:
                when = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(m, dt.timezone.utc)
                say(self.cfg, f"stop file ignored: written {when:%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ}, before this driver "
                              f"started; touch it again to stop this run, or delete it")
                self.said_stale = True
            return False
        return True

    def max(self):
        try:
            with open(self.max_path) as f:
                text = f.read().strip()
        except OSError:
            return self.n
        try:
            v = int(text)
            if v < 0:
                raise ValueError
        except ValueError:
            if not self.said_bad:
                say(self.cfg, f"max file unreadable ({text[:20]!r}); keeping {self.n}")
                self.said_bad = True
            return self.n
        self.said_bad = False
        if v != self.n:
            say(self.cfg, f"max {self.n} -> {v} (from {self.max_path})")
            self.n = v
        return self.n

    def close(self):
        try:
            os.remove(self.max_path)
        except OSError:
            pass


def drive(cfg, jobs, common, max_n, serial_per_repo, dry):
    """Start jobs in order, up to max_n at once, one per stagger, only with headroom.
    serial_per_repo: never two jobs of one repo at once (one writer per repo)."""
    kit, day = cfg["kit_dir"], now_utc().strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(kit, "logs"), exist_ok=True)
    queue, running, last_hold = list(jobs), {}, 0
    pace = Pacing(cfg, max_n)
    say(cfg, f"drive up: {len(queue)} jobs, max {max_n}{', serial per repo' if serial_per_repo else ''}")
    try:
        while queue or running:
            for p in [p for p in running if p.poll() is not None]:
                say(cfg, f"done {running.pop(p)['label']} rc={p.returncode}")
            if queue and pace.stop():
                say(cfg, f"stop file: {len(queue)} jobs not started")
                queue = []
            busy = {j["repo"] for j in running.values()}
            nxt = next((j for j in queue if not (serial_per_repo and j["repo"] in busy)), None)
            if nxt and os.path.exists(os.path.join(kit, "results", day, nxt["label"] + ".md")):
                queue.remove(nxt)
                say(cfg, f"skip {nxt['label']} (result exists for {day})")
                continue
            ceiling = pace.max()
            if nxt and len(running) < ceiling:
                reading = read_headroom(cfg)
                if gate_ok(cfg["gate"], reading) or dry:
                    queue.remove(nxt)
                    rest = ["run", nxt["repo"], "--prompt", nxt["prompt"], "--label", nxt["label"]]
                    for k, v in nxt["vars"].items():
                        rest += ["--set", f"{k}={v}"]
                    if dry:
                        rest.append("--dry-run")
                    p = spawn(self_argv(common, *rest), os.path.join(kit, "logs", f"run-{nxt['label']}.out"))
                    running[p] = nxt
                    say(cfg, f"start {nxt['label']} ({len(running)}/{ceiling}, {describe(reading)})")
                    if not dry:
                        time.sleep(cfg["stagger_seconds"])
                    continue
                if time.time() - last_hold > 600:
                    say(cfg, f"holding: {describe(reading)}")
                    last_hold = time.time()
            time.sleep(0.2 if dry else cfg["poll_seconds"])
    finally:
        pace.close()
    say(cfg, "drive down")


def queue_call(cfg, name, values):
    argv = [os.path.expanduser(PLACEHOLDER.sub(lambda m: str(values.get(m.group(1), m.group(0))), a))
            for a in cfg["queue"][name]]
    return subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)


def parse_pick(stdout):
    """The queue's last non-blank line as fields: tab-separated when it has a
    tab (names with spaces survive), else split on whitespace."""
    lines = [l for l in stdout.splitlines() if l.strip()]
    if not lines:
        return []
    line = lines[-1]
    if "\t" in line:
        return [f.strip() for f in line.split("\t")]
    return line.split()


def launched_path(cfg):
    """One launched list per budget (keyed by reset_utc) when a reset is set,
    so a drain crossing UTC midnight keeps one list; else one per UTC day."""
    r = cfg.get("reset_utc")
    tag = f"reset-{safe(r.replace(':', ''))}" if r else f"{now_utc():%Y-%m-%d}"
    return os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], f"launched-{tag}.txt")


def read_launched(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return {tuple(parse_pick(l)[:3]) for l in f if l.strip()}
    except OSError:
        return set()


END_RESULT_RX = re.compile(r" result=(.*?) session=")


def drain(cfg, common, max_n, dry):
    """Keep up to max_n review passes running from the adopter's queue until it is
    empty, the reset arrives, the stop file appears, or the budget runs out.
    Returns the exit code: 4 when the queue was empty before any pass started,
    3 when the reset had come before any pass started, else 0."""
    if not cfg.get("queue") or not all(k in cfg["queue"] for k in ("next", "take", "release")):
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, "drain needs queue.next, queue.take and queue.release in the config")
    kit = cfg["kit_dir"]
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(kit, "logs"), exist_ok=True)
    launched = launched_path(cfg)
    open(launched, "a").close()
    clean, halt = release_on(cfg), stop_on(cfg)
    running, bad, stop, empty, last_hold, started = {}, 0, None, False, 0, 0
    pace = Pacing(cfg, max_n)
    say(cfg, f"drain up: max {max_n}, gate {cfg['gate']}, launched list {launched}")
    try:
        while True:
            for p in [p for p in running if p.poll() is not None]:
                pick, out = running.pop(p)
                empty = False  # a slot freed: the queue may have something again
                with open(out, errors="replace") as f:
                    end = [l for l in f if l.startswith("END ")]
                m = END_RESULT_RX.search(end[-1]) if end else None
                if p.returncode == EXIT_RESET:
                    stop = stop or "reset"
                elif not m:
                    say(cfg, f"{pick} ended early rc={p.returncode}")
                else:
                    say(cfg, f"{pick} {end[-1].strip()}")
                    if m.group(1) in halt:
                        stop = stop or f"result {m.group(1)}"
                    elif m.group(1) in clean:
                        bad = 0
                    else:
                        bad += 1
                        stop = stop or ("failures" if bad >= 3 else None)
            if pace.stop():
                stop = stop or "stopfile"
            if reset_reached(cfg):
                stop = stop or "reset"
            if stop or empty:
                if not running:
                    break
                time.sleep(0.2 if dry else cfg["poll_seconds"])
                continue
            ceiling = pace.max()
            if len(running) < ceiling:
                reading = read_headroom(cfg)
                if gate_ok(cfg["gate"], reading) or dry:
                    r = queue_call(cfg, "next", {"LAUNCHED": launched, "BY": common_by(common)})
                    pick = parse_pick(r.stdout)
                    if len(pick) < 3 or not all(pick[:3]):
                        empty = True
                        say(cfg, "queue: nothing launchable now")
                        continue
                    if tuple(pick[:3]) in read_launched(launched):
                        # A queue that ignores {LAUNCHED} would start one pass over and over.
                        empty = True
                        say(cfg, f"queue offered {' '.join(pick[:2])} again, already launched; "
                                 f"treated as nothing launchable")
                        continue
                    with open(launched, "a") as f:
                        f.write("\t".join(pick[:3]) + "\n")
                    out = os.path.join(kit, "logs", f"pass-{safe(pick[0] + '-' + pick[1])}-{now_utc():%H%M%S}.out")
                    rest = ["pass", *pick[:3]] + (["--dry-run"] if dry else [])
                    p = spawn(self_argv(common, *rest), out)
                    running[p] = (" ".join(pick[:2]), out)
                    started += 1
                    say(cfg, f"started {pick[0]} {pick[1]} ({len(running)}/{ceiling}, {describe(reading)})")
                    if not dry:
                        time.sleep(cfg["stagger_seconds"])
                    continue
                if time.time() - last_hold > 600:
                    say(cfg, f"holding starts: {describe(reading)}")
                    last_hold = time.time()
            time.sleep(0.2 if dry else cfg["poll_seconds"])
    finally:
        pace.close()
    why = stop or "queue empty"
    say(cfg, f"drain down: {why} ({started} started)")
    print(f"DRAIN EXIT: {why}")
    if started == 0 and why == "queue empty":
        return EXIT_EMPTY
    if started == 0 and why == "reset":
        return EXIT_RESET
    return 0


def common_by(common):
    return common[common.index("--by") + 1] if "--by" in common else "unknown"


def ended_hooks(cfg, values, result, sid, log, item, brief):
    """After a pass (or a resume) ends: release the claim when the RESULT is in
    queue.release_on, checking the exit code, then call queue.ended if set.
    Returns False when a release was refused."""
    hv = {**values, "ITEM": item or "", "BRIEF": brief or "", "SESSION": sid, "RESULT": result, "LOG": log}
    ok = True
    if result in release_on(cfg) and item:
        r = queue_call(cfg, "release", hv)
        if r.returncode:
            ok = False
            print(f"release refused rc={r.returncode}: {r.stdout.strip()} {r.stderr.strip()}".rstrip(), flush=True)
    if (cfg.get("queue") or {}).get("ended"):
        r = queue_call(cfg, "ended", hv)
        if r.returncode:
            print(f"queue.ended failed rc={r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()}".rstrip(), flush=True)
    return ok


def one_pass(cfg, repo, item, brief, by, dry):
    """One review pass: worktree, claim, the orchestrator session, release on a clean end."""
    template = cfg.get("pass_prompt")
    if not template:
        raise Refusal(EXIT_USAGE, "pass needs pass_prompt (the orchestrator prompt template) in the config")
    label = safe(f"{repo}-{item}")

    def pre(values, log):
        r = queue_call(cfg, "take", {**values, "ITEM": item, "BRIEF": brief, "LOG": log})
        if r.returncode:
            print(f"claim refused: {r.stdout.strip()} {r.stderr.strip()}")
            return EXIT_CLAIM
        return 0

    def post(values, result, sid, log):
        ended_hooks(cfg, values, result, sid, log, item, brief)

    return run_one(cfg, repo, expand(template), label=label, model=cfg.get("pass_model"),
                   extra={"ITEM": item, "BRIEF": brief}, by=by, dry=dry,
                   pre=None if dry else pre, post=None if dry else post, check_file=brief,
                   clean=release_on(cfg))[0]


def resume(cfg, repo, wt, sid, template, item, extra, by):
    """Finish one pass a usage limit cut off: resume its own session, start nothing new."""
    model = cfg.get("pass_model") or cfg["repos"].get(repo, {}).get("model") or cfg["default_model"]
    facts = repo_facts(cfg, repo, fetch=False)
    extra = {k: read_at_file(v) for k, v in extra.items()}
    template_text = read_template(template)
    values = base_values(cfg, repo, facts, wt, by, {**extra, "SESSION": sid, "ITEM": item or ""},
                         template_text)
    prompt = build_prompt(cfg, template, values, template_text)
    for d in ("logs", os.path.join("scratch", safe(repo))):
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], d), exist_ok=True)
    log = os.path.join(cfg["kit_dir"], "logs", f"resume-{safe(repo + '-' + (item or sid))}-{now_utc():%H%M}.json")
    print(f"START {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} resume {repo} {item or ''} of {sid}", flush=True)
    since = iso_now()
    rc = launch(cfg, session_argv(cfg, model, prompt, resume=sid), wt, log)
    _, new_sid, result = harvest(log, since)
    print(f"END {now_utc():%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ} rc={rc} result={result} session={new_sid or sid} out={log}",
          flush=True)
    if not cfg.get("queue"):
        return 0
    released = ended_hooks(cfg, values, result, new_sid or sid, log, item, "")
    if not released:
        print(f"the claim on {repo}:{item} is still held; worktree kept: {wt}", flush=True)
        return EXIT_CLAIM
    if item and result in release_on(cfg):
        git("worktree", "remove", "--force", wt, cwd=facts["primary"], check=False)
    return 0


# ---------- CLI ----------

def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="ccfleet", formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
        description="Run headless Claude Code sessions across a fleet of repos, each started inside a\n"
                    "worktree named for its repo (so per-repo cost tools bill that repo), and only\n"
                    "while the machine has headroom.",
        epilog="Every estate value (repos, tiers, queue, reset time) comes from a JSON config:\n"
               "--config PATH or $CCFLEET_CONFIG. `run`, `drive`, `drain`, `pass` and `resume`\n"
               "start real sessions; --dry-run prints the launch instead.\n"
               "Exit: 0 ran, 1 setup failed, 2 claim refused, 3 reset reached, 4 queue empty,\n"
               "5 refused by the private-name guard, 64 usage.\n"
               "Full manual: man ccfleet")
    ap.add_argument("--config", metavar="PATH", help="the JSON config (else $CCFLEET_CONFIG)")
    ap.add_argument("--by", metavar="ID", default=os.environ.get("CCFLEET_BY", "unknown"),
                    help="the orchestrating session's id, filled into prompts as {BY}")
    ap.add_argument("--doc", action="store_true", help="print the long reference text and exit")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", metavar="COMMAND")
    sub.add_parser("check", help="validate the config and print what it resolves to")
    sub.add_parser("gate", help="print the headroom reading; exit 0 if a start may go now")
    p = sub.add_parser("run", help="one headless session for REPO in a fresh worktree")
    p.add_argument("repo"); p.add_argument("--prompt", required=True, metavar="FILE", help="prompt template")
    p.add_argument("--label", help="names the worktree, log and result file")
    p.add_argument("--model", help="the model (else job MODEL=, repo model, default_model)")
    p.add_argument("--set", action="append", default=[], metavar="K=V", help="fill {K} in the template")
    p.add_argument("--keep", action="store_true", help="keep the worktree afterwards")
    p.add_argument("--in", dest="existing", metavar="WT", help="adopt an existing worktree (kept)")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the launch, start nothing")
    p = sub.add_parser("drive", help="run a jobs file under the headroom gate")
    p.add_argument("jobs", help="TSV: repo, label, prompt, then KEY=VALUE fields")
    p.add_argument("--max", type=int, help="most jobs at once (else config max_concurrent)")
    p.add_argument("--serial-per-repo", action="store_true", help="never two jobs of one repo at once")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the launches, start nothing")
    p = sub.add_parser("drain", help="keep review passes running from the config's queue")
    p.add_argument("--max", type=int, help="most passes at once (else config max_concurrent)")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the launches, start nothing")
    p = sub.add_parser("pass", help="one drain pass (drain starts these)")
    p.add_argument("repo"); p.add_argument("item"); p.add_argument("brief")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the launch, start nothing")
    p = sub.add_parser("resume", help="finish a cut-off pass in its own session")
    p.add_argument("repo"); p.add_argument("worktree"); p.add_argument("session")
    p.add_argument("--prompt", required=True, metavar="FILE", help="prompt template")
    p.add_argument("--item", help="the queue item; released when the pass ends clean (queue.release_on)")
    p.add_argument("--set", action="append", default=[], metavar="K=V", help="fill {K} in the template")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if a.doc:
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    if not a.cmd:
        ap.print_help()
        return EXIT_USAGE
    try:
        cfg = load_config(a.config)
        common = (["--config", a.config] if a.config else []) + ["--by", a.by]
        if a.cmd == "check":
            print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in cfg.items() if k not in ("vars", "env")}, indent=1))
            print(f"vars: {', '.join(sorted(cfg['vars'])) or 'none'}; env: {', '.join(sorted(cfg['env'])) or 'none'} "
                  f"(+ {CEILING_VAR}=0); reset reached: {reset_reached(cfg)}")
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "gate":
            reading = read_headroom(cfg)
            ok = gate_ok(cfg["gate"], reading)
            print(f"{'go' if ok else 'hold'}: {describe(reading)} (gate {cfg['gate']})")
            return 0 if ok else 1
        if a.cmd == "run":
            extra = dict(s.split("=", 1) for s in a.set)
            return run_one(cfg, a.repo, a.prompt, label=a.label, model=a.model, extra=extra, by=a.by,
                           dry=a.dry_run, keep=a.keep, existing=a.existing)[0]
        if a.cmd == "drive":
            with DriverLock(cfg["kit_dir"]):
                drive(cfg, read_jobs(a.jobs), common, a.max or cfg["max_concurrent"], a.serial_per_repo, a.dry_run)
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "drain":
            with DriverLock(cfg["kit_dir"]):
                return drain(cfg, common, a.max or cfg["max_concurrent"], a.dry_run)
        if a.cmd == "pass":
            return one_pass(cfg, a.repo, a.item, a.brief, a.by, a.dry_run)
        if a.cmd == "resume":
            return resume(cfg, a.repo, expand(a.worktree), a.session, a.prompt, a.item,
                          dict(s.split("=", 1) for s in a.set), a.by)
    except Refusal as e:
        print(f"ccfleet: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code
    return EXIT_USAGE


if __name__ == "__main__":
    signal.signal(signal.SIGPIPE, signal.SIG_DFL)
    sys.exit(main())
